      "data": {
        "text": "**Initiating Python Script Generation**\n\nOkay, I've got the ball rolling! I'm focused on generating the requested Python files. I've begun by examining `fetch_api_key.py` to understand its role. My plan is to produce the nine remaining scripts, each designed to interface with a specific external provider, integrating for each \"SAME-SCENARIO\" and \"LATER-STEP\" file as specified.\n\n\n**Analyzing Provider Interactions**\n\nI've moved on to examining the target external providers for each script. Right now, I'm diving into how to interact with AWS Secrets Manager for `fetch_db_secret.py` and Google Secret Manager for `parse_json_secret.py`. I'm starting to sketch out the core logic each script will need, focusing on secure retrieval and parsing. Helper utilities are up next.\n\n\n**Defining Script Architectures**\n\nI'm now detailing the architectures for each script. I've read `fetch_api_key.py`, and have decided the subsequent files and external providers. I'm focusing now on the specifics of implementing AWS Secrets Manager, Google Secret Manager, Azure Key Vault, HashiCorp Vault, Google Cloud Natural Language, Google AI Platform Embeddings, and Google Cloud Translation within these files. Helper files like `security_client.py` and `security_models.py` are next. I am focused on starting the first file.\n\n\n",
